<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chu–Han Contention</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chu-Han War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chu-Han Contention was the civil war that followed the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin dynasty</a> in the late third century BCE, fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> of Chu and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a> of Han. Liu Bang emerged victorious and proclaimed himself emperor. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chu-han-contention.jpg" alt="Chu–Han Contention" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chu-Han_Contention.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
